---
import BaseLayout from '../../components/BaseLayout.astro';
import DataTable from '../../components/DataTable.astro';
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Standards"
  description="Standards topics map: every layer of the UniDPP framework with its mechanisms and steward body, the layer seams, and the profile landscape."
  eyebrow="04 · Reference — standards"
>
  <h1>Standards</h1>
  <p class="lede">
    Every layer the framework offers is ISO/IEC/UN-neutral and already exists as a
    standard, a dataset, or a running system. The table below maps each layer to its
    mechanisms and its steward; nothing in the framework depends on a proprietary
    mechanism.
  </p>

  <section id="topics-map" class="plate" aria-labelledby="topics-h">
    <h2 id="topics-h">Topics map</h2>
    <DataTable
      columns={['Layer', 'Mechanisms', 'Steward']}
      rows={[
        ['Identity', 'ISO/IEC 15459 issuance; bridges to GS1, Handle (工业互联网标识解析), Ecode, and MA schemes', 'ISO/IEC JTC 1/SC 31 lineage; TC 154 registry bindings'],
        ['Carrier', 'ISO/IEC 18004, 16022, 18000-3/-63, 18092; GS1 Digital Link + RFC 9264 linksets; IEC 61406 identity links', 'SC 31; GS1; IEC'],
        ['Core model', 'EXPRESS (ISO 10303-11) with derived JSON and XML renders; expressir validation', 'ELF'],
        ['Registry', 'ISO 19135:2025 / FERIN federated registers; UNTDED seed dataset; CDDAL dictionary technology (OpenCDD)', 'Enosema; TC 154 / UN/CEFACT; ELF'],
        ['Rules, transforms, twin', 'Prellel executable-regulation packages; Primmel SMART twin runtime and twin-cert; Confium threshold PKI', 'OIML SMART programme (programme-agnostic ladder)'],
        ['Trust', 'SIGNATIF: trust DAG, threshold roots, transparency logs, algorithm agility, co-signatures; CNML as post-quantum ESDC realization', 'CalConnect + TC 154; OIML'],
        ['Cryptographic suites', 'SM2/SM3/SM4/SM9 (ISO/IEC 14888-3, 10118-3, 18033-3), FIPS suites, ML-DSA — profile-bound, co-signed', 'Per jurisdiction; registry-governed'],
        ['Time and events', 'ISO 8601-1/-2 incl. Amd1; ISO 34000 vocabulary; temporal profile; event model', 'CalConnect'],
        ['Units and quantities', 'ISO 80000 → UnitsDB/UnitsML; isq-smart; OpenCDD unit mirror', 'CalConnect (UnitsML); isq-smart; ELF'],
        ['API', 'EN 18222 as the EU-profile API; freeDPP as an open implementation reference', 'CEN-CLC/JTC 24 profile; community'],
        ['Twin sources', 'Pimmel SMART (reference implementation); UNTP mapping; AAS one informative mapping only', 'UniDPP; UNECE; IDTA'],
      ]}
    />
  </section>

  <section id="eu-profile" aria-labelledby="eu-h">
    <h2 id="eu-h">The EU profile</h2>
    <p>
      The European series — EN 18216 through EN 18246 — and the ESPR delegated acts are
      treated as exactly one jurisdiction profile, on equal footing with every other: EN
      18219 identifiers, EN 18220 carriers, EN 18221 persistence, EN 18222 APIs, EN 18223
      content, EN 18239 roles, EN 18246 verification. The series’ own neutrality language
      (“technology, ontology and domain agnostic”, EN 18223 §0.3; “without vendor
      lock-in”, EN 18216 scope) is implemented rather than amended. Known vacancies — the
      semantic repository at EN 18223 §4.3 and the event/time model behind §4.2’s mandated
      change logging — are addressed by the
      <a href="/reference/papers/">registry and lifecycle contributions</a>.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section id="seams" class="plate" aria-labelledby="seams-h">
    <h2 id="seams-h">Seams</h2>
    <p>
      Layers join at twelve seams. They are tracked as first-class engineering surfaces
      because seam failures are where the system cracks: every defect recorded in the audit
      of the EN series is a seam failure.
    </p>
    <DataTable
      columns={['Seam', 'Joint']}
      rows={[
        ['S1', 'Carrier ↔ resolver — code-format translation; 1D-to-2D migration.'],
        ['S2', 'Resolver ↔ hosts — mirrors, national intermediary layers, dark identities.'],
        ['<strong>S3</strong>', '<strong>Core ↔ profiles — the mount, where neutrality is enforced.</strong>'],
        ['S4', 'Profile ↔ registry — <code>dictionaryReference</code> protocol, version pinning.'],
        ['S5', 'Registry ↔ registry — FERIN federation, CDDAL canonicalization.'],
        ['S6', 'Event log ↔ transparency logs — commitment anchoring, salt discipline.'],
        ['S7', 'Issuer credentials ↔ profile trust lists — delegation DAG, roots, master list.'],
        ['S8', 'Transforms ↔ engines — Prellel packages; determinism; version pinned at verification time.'],
        ['S9', 'Parent ↔ child passports — installation edges, blind modes, mixed-profile children.'],
        ['S10', 'Device ↔ system — edge commit/reveal; contact dumps.'],
        ['S11', 'Tier A ↔ Tier B — embedded minimum vs served; staleness marking.'],
        ['S12', 'Passport ↔ adjacent regimes — customs/WCO, e-invoicing, EPCIS/UNTP, CIDOC-CRM, ISO 20022.'],
      ]}
    />
  </section>

  <section id="profile-landscape" aria-labelledby="landscape-h">
    <h2 id="landscape-h">Profile landscape</h2>
    <p>
      Profiles are authored by regulators through national standards bodies and
      registration authorities, and are onboarded through the FERIN template and a
      SIGNATIF trust-onboarding ceremony.
    </p>
    <ul>
      <li>
        <strong>Jurisdiction profiles:</strong> EU ESPR delegated acts (textiles 2026;
        steel 30/07/2027; registry implementing act 30/06/2027); CN CCC/GB with SM
        cryptographic suites; JP METI/PSE/Top Runner; KR KC; US state and
        federal-procurement law; UK UKCA.
      </li>
      <li>
        <strong>Sector overlays:</strong> electronics, textiles, batteries, construction,
        tyres, packaging; measuring instruments as the OIML pilot vertical.
      </li>
      <li>
        <strong>Characteristic profiles:</strong> CITES species content; cultural goods
        (EU 2019/880); art-market AML; conflict minerals; CRMA; end-of-waste; recycled
        content; historic vehicles; voluntary provenance and grading for antiques and
        collectibles.
      </li>
      <li>
        <strong>Carrier and presentation profiles:</strong> GB/T 33993; WeChat
        mini-program channel.
      </li>
    </ul>
  </section>

  <section id="mappings" aria-labelledby="mappings-h">
    <h2 id="mappings-h">Mappings (informative)</h2>
    <p>
      UNTP; EPCIS; ISO 59040; and AAS — one informative mapping, with a drift monitor, in
      line with the doctrine that AAS is not load-bearing. Informative mappings are
      published for interoperability and are never a dependency of any invariant.
    </p>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>
